    1. pick grid size H, W each uniformly from 6-16
    2. pick marker count N from 1-3
    3. pick N distinct colors from {red, green, teal}
    4. place markers one at a time at random positions in [1, H-2] x [1, W-2]
    5. reject/retry a position if its 3x3 neighborhood overlaps any previously placed marker's 3x3 neighborhood (Chebyshev distance < 3 between centers)
    6. grid is all black except the N marker pixels
